        {
          "text": "What it is"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "key": "b2",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "E471 (mono- and diglycerides of fatty acids) are emulsifiers made from glycerol and fatty acids, which may be plant- or animal-derived. They blend fat and water and improve texture in baked goods, spreads and more."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "key": "b3",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why it is in your food"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "key": "b4",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Manufacturers use it as emulsifier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "key": "b5",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What we hold on it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "key": "b6",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This page is about the record we hold on this additive: who has written about it, and where you can read them."
